Economy Design Analysis
Aion 2 Global: Economy, RMT, and Player Retention

Problem Statement

Current anti-RMT strategies focus heavily on enforcement while failing to address economic incentives driving player participation.

Key Observations

Currency sellers remain profitable.
Players choose cheaper alternatives when official acquisition paths become frustrating.
Auction houses can unintentionally facilitate wealth transfers.

Design Question

How can the game reduce demand for illicit currency rather than solely punish supply?

Proposed Solutions

Increased accessibility of progression resources.
Dynamic market monitoring.
Economic sink balancing.
Reduced friction for legitimate players.

